 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Sure, what age is the oldest three years old? That's a lot of mouths to feed. Do you have a designated leader? Cut them into boxes instead of whole ones. Each kid gets box, and they can eat from their own knife. A treasure hunt, spotting birds, and building a sand castle keep them busy. A big tent and lots of drinks will keep most of the sun off. Pack the chairs away from the others, and have one person in charge of fire. It's small group, so a few torches do the trick.",
